===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|grammar}} The [[accusative case]].
# {{lb|en|grammar}} A [[word]] [[inflected]] in the [[accusative case]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Hans Reichelt|title=Avesta Reader: Texts, Notes, Glossary and Index|location=Strassburg<t:Strasbourg>|publisher=Verlag von Karl J. Trübner|year=1911|page=105|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/39002003156933.med.yale.edu/page/105/mode/1up|passage=65 ''mošu tat̰ ās nōit̮ darəγəm yat̰'' .&nbsp;. ‘quickly it (''tat̰'') happened, it (was) not long till .&nbsp;.&nbsp;. — ''drūm avantəm airištəm'': according to Bartholomae IF. ''12''. 146 the author of this part was led to use '''accusatives''' here (instead of nominatives) by the preceding sentence ''yezi ǰum frapayeni''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:W. F. Jackson Knight|W[illiam] F[rancis] Jackson Knight]]|chapter=Language, Verse, and Style|title=Roman Vergil|series=Peregrine Books|location=Harmondsworth|publisher=w:Penguin Books|year=1944|year_published=1966|page=265|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/wfjacksonknight0000unse/page/265/mode/1up|passage=There is some antecedent in old Latin; but as usual the influence is Greek too, for Greek prose and poetry freely use '''accusatives''' which are to some extent adverbial '''accusatives''', or '''accusatives''' of respect.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Mily Crevels; Peter Bakker|chapter=External Possession in Romani|editors=Viktor Elšík; w:Yaron Matras|title=Grammatical Relations in Romani: The Noun Phrase|series=Amsterdam Studies in the Theory and History of Linguistic Science: Series IV – Current Issues in Linguistic Theory|seriesvolume=211|location=Amsterdam; Philadelphia, Pa.|publisher=w:John Benjamins Publishing Company|year=2000|page=181|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/grammaticalrelat0000unse/page/181/mode/1up|passage=Romani distinguishes dative and accusative pronouns ''formally'' and some Romani dialects use '''accusatives''' in constructions in which other languages employ a dative.}}

